- rd/low_interlaced (B84): interlaced input, png_set_interlace_handling, loop passes.
- rd/low_interlaced_manual (B85): interlaced input WITHOUT png_set_interlace_handling.
- rd/rows_api (B86): png_read_rows with row only, display_row only, and both.
- rd/prog_* (B91-B94): png_set_progressive_read_fn + png_process_data fed in chunk sizes 1,2,3,7,13,64,1024 and whole; prog_pause uses png_process_data_pause(save=0 and 1); prog_partial_cbs passes None for some callbacks.
- rd/simple_* (B95-B99): png_image_begin_read_from_memory + png_image_finish_read over the PNG_FORMAT_* cross product (ALPHA|COLOR|LINEAR|COLORMAP|BGR|AFIRST). Print the return value, warning_or_error, msg(), and emit_bytes of the output buffer AND the colormap. Always memset the png_image to zero and set version=PNG_IMAGE_VERSION, opaque=null. Call png_image_free afterwards.
- rd/tr_* (B100-B137): one read transform per case, applied to the color types it makes sense for; record decoded rows AND the post-update_info rowbytes/channels/bit_depth/color_type.
- rd/tr_pipelines (B137): the 7 composed pipelines listed in CONFIGS.md row 137.
- rd/crc_action_grid (B139): build a stream with a bad ancillary CRC and one with a bad critical CRC (helper `chunk_badcrc`), loop crit_action 0..5 x ancil_action 0..5. A bad critical CRC is fatal, so use `variant()` to put each grid cell in its own process, or set only the ancillary case in-process.
- rd/chunk_cache_max / chunk_malloc_max / user_limits / opt_* / keep_unknown / user_chunk_fn / mem_fn / sig_bytes: see rows B140-B151. For rd/mem_fn install malloc/free callbacks that just call libc malloc/free via `extern "C" { fn malloc(n: usize) -> *mut c_void; fn free(p: *mut c_void); }` and COUNT the calls, printing only the count (never an address).
- rd/sig_bytes (B151): consume n bytes of the signature yourself, then png_set_sig_bytes(n) and feed the remainder.
- rd/idat_split (B155): rebuild the stream splitting the zlib data across 1,2,5 IDAT chunks and include a zero-length IDAT.
- rd/roundtrip_* (B156-B158): write then read back, comparing both the encoded bytes and the decoded rows.
- rd/io_state (B163): sample png_get_io_state and png_get_io_chunk_type from inside the read callback and print the whole sequence.

