[38;5;252m[1m## Two real translation bugs found and fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both were the same class: Rust's [38;5;10m/[0m panics on a zero divisor where C takes the hardware divide fault.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
1. [38;5;10mpng_image_write_to_memory[0m with [38;5;10mwidth == 0[0m ([38;5;10msrc/pngwrite2.rs:606[0m) — C raised [38;5;10mSIGFPE[0m (exit 136), Rust aborted via panic (exit 134).[0m[0m
2. The same expression on the read side, [38;5;10mpng_image_finish_read[0m ([38;5;10msrc/pngread3.rs:1456[0m).[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Fixed with a new [38;5;10mc_div_u32[0m helper in [38;5;10msrc/helpers.rs[0m that issues the raw division instruction, reproducing C's fault exactly. I deliberately did [3mnot[23m add a guard the C lacks — that would itself be a divergence. An audit of the remaining eight variable-divisor sites confirmed each is guarded in the C exactly as in the Rust.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## How the harness works[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Because [38;5;10mpng_error[0m never returns to its caller, each case runs in a [1mworker subprocess[22m per library; the driver spawns both, then compares stdout [3mand[23m exit status/signal byte-for-byte. That avoids [38;5;10msetjmp[0m from Rust entirely and makes the terminating signal part of the assertion — which is how the divide-fault difference surfaced. Transcripts are written through unbuffered so they survive a crash and are still compared up to the fault point.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Both libraries are reached [1monly[22m through [38;5;10mlibloading[0m, so the [38;5;10m#[no_mangle][0m wrappers are under test. 335 of the 384 exported symbols are called directly, including libpng's internal [38;5;10mPNG_INTERNAL_*[0m helpers (this build has no visibility script, so they're part of the ABI); the remaining 49 need a [38;5;10mpng_struct[0m in a specific mid-operation state and are covered through the pipeline.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Also worth flagging[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc_src/CMakeLists.txt[0m links only zlib, so the reference [38;5;10m.so[0m leaves [38;5;10mfloor[0m and [38;5;10mpow[0m undefined and cannot be loaded at all. Since [38;5;10mc_src/[0m is read-only, I linked libm into the test driver instead — a [38;5;10mdlopen[0med object resolves from the global scope. Without this, every floating-point path (gamma, cHRM, sCAL, the whole simplified API) would have been silently untestable; 16 read cases and 6 write cases were failing purely on this.[0m[0m
